Silicon captures from an RTX 3090 (GA102, SM86), taken by patching one instruction word into nvcc-compiled seed kernels and reading the registers back through the CUDA driver API.
One fixture per line, id is <capture>#<index in that capture> and word_hex the instruction.
observed:true means the outputs were captured on silicon, false marks a case that could not be run.
The ids are what the known-failure lists in core/src/tests/gpu/fixtures.rs refer to.
mul-add and gradient are whole nvcc-compiled programs with their silicon outputs.
guest/guest.bin is the flat AArch64 image scripts/build-guest.sh builds from guest/ for core/src/guest.rs, sha256 86dcbf2e50a3a4d80fdddd0c855c2e874376975caade469d57bc0830f190b33c.
driver-shaders holds NVIDIA driver 580 SM86 output (RTX A6000, Vulkan pipeline cache) for demos/shaders and a minimal pass-through triangle pair: each graphics file is the 0x80-byte program header followed by the code, the compute file is code only.
query-{candidates,hit,address,flags}.comp.bin are the rig's GL_EXT_ray_query compute shaders, compiled by NVIDIA driver 580 for an RTX 3090; they cover candidate confirmation, opaque hits, a push-constant TLAS address and ray flags.
rt.vert.bin and rt.frag.bin are pbr.vert and rt.frag (area-light shadows, mirror, glass and glossy reflections, AO and one-bounce light from both lights), and pbr.frag.bin is pbr.frag with its fill and rim lights, compiled by NVIDIA driver 580.126.20 on an RTX 3090. Bank 0x1d holds texture handles at +0, the TLAS at +0x18 and the uniform-buffer handle at +0x28.
